  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you're ready to finish your basement and put up some walls, which is awesome! But wait—before you even think about studs and drywall, we absolutely have to talk about moisture. This is probably the most crucial step, and honestly, if you skip it, you're setting yourself up for headaches like mold and damaged finishes down the road. First, take a good, hard look for any leaks, damp spots, or that white powdery stuff called efflorescence. These are all signs of water intrusion. You'll want to get your exterior drainage sorted out first—think downspouts, grading, and all that good stuff to steer water away from your foundation. Sometimes, it's as simple as sealing a few cracks. You really need to let everything dry out completely before you even think about bringing lumber into the space. If you've got persistent moisture issues, or you're not sure how to properly waterproof, that's definitely a situation where a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can step in and help assess the situation. Getting this right from the start means your framed walls will stay dry and healthy for years to come. Don't frame over a problem; fix it first!"
    }
  ],
